# std - the CT standard library, published as a normal ct-pkg package.
#
# The repository root is the package root; the `std/` directory under it is the
# namespace root, so `-I vendor/std` resolves `import std::<mod>::<Unit>`.
#
# Version policy: 0.x means the surface may break in a minor bump. See README.md.
#
# `requires` is measured, not guessed. Literal receivers (`"/tmp/x".open("r")`,
# `"abc".len()`) are rejected by v0.19.1 with "method receiver must be a
# variable, an element, a call or a field chain", so 0.20.0 is the floor for
# that feature. `std::io` names its handle with a type alias
# (`pub type IoFile = struct ct_io_file;`), and type aliases only parse from
# 0.20.3 on.
#
# 0.3.0 raises the floor to 0.30.0: `Vec<T>` / `Map<K,V>` / `MapEntry<K,V>`
# became the compiler's built-in layer in v0.30.0 (ct-lang Phase 29, released
# with v0.30.0; `lib/std/Vec.h.ct` plus the reserved-name check at
# `Parser.h.ct`'s "is a built-in type and cannot be redeclared"), and this
# package no longer ships `std::vec` / `std::map`. On 0.20.3..0.29.x there is
# no built-in container layer, so a consumer would lose the containers
# entirely -- hence the raised floor rather than the old 0.20.3.
#
# The version line restarted at 0.1.0; 0.1.0 also adds `std::io` (printf, puts,
# putchar, getchar, fflush, and file open/read/write/close) next to `std::num`
# and `std::math`. `-lm` rides in `ldflags` because std::math calls sqrt / fabs
# / isnan / isinf; on platforms where libm is part of libc it is a no-op, on
# the others it is required.
#
# `publisher` and `ns-root` are the two keys the replacement package mechanism
# requires (SP-002 / SP-003 in ct-lang's ct-pkg-shared-store requirements).
# Measured on ct v0.53.0: both are accepted with no diagnostic and silently
# ignored -- unknown keys in `ct.pkg` are skipped by `read_manifest` -- so
# `ct build` and `tests/run.sh` behave byte-for-byte as before. They are
# declared here so the manifest already carries the package identity: the
# include root is the package root itself, hence `ns-root = .` (the `std/`
# segment of `import std::<mod>::<Unit>` comes from the directory tree under
# it, not from this key).
name = std
publisher = std
ns-root = .
version = 0.5.0
licence = MIT
requires = ct >= 0.30.0
ldflags = -lm
